{
  "id": "COMPOUND:17374 - PROTEIN:5347",
  "verbalization": "Mollicellin N is implicated in the regulation of CP50-MEL-B through multiple pathways, with the most direct link emerging through its interaction with P2X purinoceptors. The evidence suggests that Mollicellin N acts as a target for two distinct P2X purinoceptor subtypes, P2X 1 and P2X 7, which are both targeted by a common compound [(1R)-1-[(5Z)-4-Bromo-5-(Bromomethylidene)-2-Oxofuran-3-Yl]Butyl] Acetate. This compound is known to interact with P2X receptors and ultimately modulate the activity of CP50-MEL-B. The presence of a shared target compound and the involvement of P2X receptors in the pathway supports a mechanistic link between Mollicellin N and CP50-MEL-B, particularly through the activation of these receptors. The evidence is consistent with a role for Mollicellin N in regulating P2X receptor function, which in turn influences CP50-MEL-B activity. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism by which Mollicellin N may exert its effects on CP50-MEL-B, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the exact nature of the interaction.",
